### Orbit Eats API - manual requests (VS Code extension "REST Client")
### Click "Send Request" above each request. Start the API first: python app.py

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@token = Bearer token-secreto-123

### 1. Without token -> 401 (NFR-02)
GET {{base}}/customers

### 2. List customers
GET {{base}}/customers
Authorization: {{token}}

### 3. Create a customer -> 201 (change the email if it already exists)
POST {{base}}/customers
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Sofia",
  "last_name": "Andrade",
  "address": "Av. Colon E5-20",
  "phone": "0984445566",
  "email": "sofia.andrade@mail.com"
}

### 4. Same email again -> 409
POST {{base}}/customers
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Sofia",
  "last_name": "Andrade",
  "address": "Av. Colon E5-20",
  "phone": "0984445566",
  "email": "sofia.andrade@mail.com"
}

### 5. Create an order with 2 products -> 201, total calculated by the API
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": 1,
  "delivery_address": "Av. Amazonas N24-10",
  "items": [
    {"product_id": 1, "quantity": 2},
    {"product_id": 2, "quantity": 1}
  ]
}

### 6. Change status and assign the delivery employee (use the order_id from request 5)
PATCH {{base}}/orders/1
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "on_the_way",
  "employee_id": 1
}

### 7. Invalid status -> 400 (CHECK constraint)
PATCH {{base}}/orders/1
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "lost"
}

### 8. Recipe of product 1 (FR-03)
GET {{base}}/products/1/recipe
Authorization: {{token}}

### 9. Ingredients below minimum stock (FR-04)
GET {{base}}/ingredients/low-stock
Authorization: {{token}}

### 10. Suppliers of ingredient 2 (FR-05)
GET {{base}}/ingredients/2/suppliers
Authorization: {{token}}
